{"id":3683,"date":"2018-10-29T14:29:04","date_gmt":"2018-10-29T18:29:04","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/ibafflatusdesign.space\/?p=3683"},"modified":"2019-09-17T18:09:27","modified_gmt":"2019-09-17T22:09:27","slug":"nord-pas-de-calais-france","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/travel-log\/nord-pas-de-calais-france\/","title":{"rendered":"Nord-Pas-De-Calais, France"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>If you ask a French person from outside of the two most northern regions what is in the north of France, they will tell you nothing besides mines and rain. And they would be correct to some extent. Yet, while the north is famous for its mines and rainy weather, it is also famous for the part that it played in the First World War. Besides the two most notable cities\u2014<a href = \u201chttp:\/\/ibafflatusdesign.space\/travel-log\/lille-france\/\u201d><u>Lille<\/u><\/a> and <a href = \u201chttp:\/\/ibafflatusdesign.space\/travel-log\/dunkirk-france\/\u201d><u>Dunkirk<\/u><\/a>&#8211;the interesting locations are Wambrechies&#8211;a city in the Nord department&#8211;and Notre-Dame-de-Lorette and Vimy (under the <i>Pas de Calais<\/i> tab).<\/p>\n<div class=\"su-tabs su-tabs-style-default su-tabs-mobile-stack\" data-active=\"1\" data-scroll-offset=\"0\" data-anchor-in-url=\"no\"><div class=\"su-tabs-nav\"><span class=\"\" data-url=\"\" data-target=\"blank\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\">Wambrechies<\/span><span class=\"\" data-url=\"\" data-target=\"blank\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\">Pas de Calais<\/span><\/div><div class=\"su-tabs-panes\"><div class=\"su-tabs-pane su-u-clearfix su-u-trim\" data-title=\"Wambrechies\">\n<style type=\"text\/css\">\r\n\t#foogallery-gallery-4375 .fg-image {\r\n        width: 150px;\r\n    }\r\n<\/style>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"foogallery foogallery-container foogallery-default foogallery-lightbox-foobox fg-gutter-10 fg-center fg-default fg-light fg-border-thin fg-shadow-outline fg-loading-default fg-loaded-fade-in fg-caption-hover fg-hover-fade fg-hover-zoom fg-ready\" id=\"foogallery-gallery-4375\" data-foogallery=\"{&quot;item&quot;:{&quot;showCaptionTitle&quot;:true,&quot;showCaptionDescription&quot;:true},&quot;lazy&quot;:true}\" >\r\n\t<div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190407_171840.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The city of Wambrechies is thought to have been born in the 6th century. The city originally drew many wealthy families who wanted to take advantage of the fresh air. In the 19th century, many more people were drawn to the city due to its prospering textile industry. It was as a result of this growth in population that this building was erected to serve as the town hall. Now, Wambrechies is a quaint town on the edge of the Deule.\" data-attachment-id=\"4383\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The city of Wambrechies is thought to have been born in the 6th century. The city originally drew many wealthy families who wanted to take advantage of the fresh air. In the 19th century, many more people were drawn to the city due to its prospering textile industry. It was as a result of this growth in population that this building was erected to serve as the town hall. Now, Wambrechies is a quaint town on the edge of the Deule.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/06\/20190407_171840\/1038324107.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The city of Wambrechies is thought to have been born in the 6th century. The city originally drew many wealthy families who wanted to take advantage of the fresh air. In the 19th century, many more people were drawn to the city due to its prospering textile industry. It was as a result of this growth in population that this building was erected to serve as the town hall. Now, Wambrechies is a quaint town on the edge of the Deule.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190407_170910.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The Claeyssens distillery was created in 1817 by a Belgian named Guillaume Claeyssens. This distillery is only one of three in France that use juniper. Wambrechies also has an alcohol with that name, which is produced in this distillery.\" data-attachment-id=\"4381\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The Claeyssens distillery was created in 1817 by a Belgian named Guillaume Claeyssens. This distillery is only one of three in France that use juniper. Wambrechies also has an alcohol with that name, which is produced in this distillery.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/06\/20190407_170910\/3977183360.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The Claeyssens distillery was created in 1817 by a Belgian named Guillaume Claeyssens. This distillery is only one of three in France that use juniper. Wambrechies also has an alcohol with that name, which is produced in this distillery.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190407_171250.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"As of 1999, this distillery is classified as a historic building and everything is kept in the most authentic style, including this courtyard.\" data-attachment-id=\"4382\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"As of 1999, this distillery is classified as a historic building and everything is kept in the most authentic style, including this courtyard.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/06\/20190407_171250\/1738646876.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">As of 1999, this distillery is classified as a historic building and everything is kept in the most authentic style, including this courtyard.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190407_155146.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"This castle, the &lt;i&gt;ch\u00e2teau de Robersart&lt;\/i&gt;, dates from 1760 and is the replacement of one built in the 1500s, which collapsed. While it was once a home for the city&#039;s noble family, it is now the property of the city. The city bought the castle to restore it and turned it into a cultural center, housing among other things the Museum of Dolls and Historic Toys.\" data-attachment-id=\"4377\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"This castle, the &lt;i&gt;ch\u00e2teau de Robersart&lt;\/i&gt;, dates from 1760 and is the replacement of one built in the 1500s, which collapsed. While it was once a home for the city&#039;s noble family, it is now the property of the city. The city bought the castle to restore it and turned it into a cultural center, housing among other things the Museum of Dolls and Historic Toys.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/06\/20190407_155146\/753249993.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">This castle, the <i>ch\u00e2teau de Robersart<\/i>, dates from 1760 and is the replacement of one built in the 1500s, which collapsed. While it was once a home for the city's noble family, it is now the property of the city. The city bought the castle to restore it and turned it into a cultural center, housing among other things the Museum of Dolls and Historic Toys.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190407_151943.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"While small, the Museum of Dolls and Historic Toys offers the unique opportunity to play with the toys that gave birth to today&#039;s billiards table.\" data-attachment-id=\"4376\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"While small, the Museum of Dolls and Historic Toys offers the unique opportunity to play with the toys that gave birth to today&#039;s billiards table.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/06\/20190407_151943\/2635080582.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">While small, the Museum of Dolls and Historic Toys offers the unique opportunity to play with the toys that gave birth to today's billiards table.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190407_160217.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"In front of the ch\u00e2teau de Robersart is the city center. It borders the Deule and features the Church of Saint Vaast (on the left). The city center was recently rebuilt to offer more comfortable amenities for tourists. During the summer people can come on boat to enjoy these new shops. In fact, it is only a thirty-minute boat ride on the Deule from Lille.\" data-attachment-id=\"4378\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"In front of the ch\u00e2teau de Robersart is the city center. It borders the Deule and features the Church of Saint Vaast (on the left). The city center was recently rebuilt to offer more comfortable amenities for tourists. During the summer people can come on boat to enjoy these new shops. In fact, it is only a thirty-minute boat ride on the Deule from Lille.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/06\/20190407_160217\/2807804240.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">In front of the ch\u00e2teau de Robersart is the city center. It borders the Deule and features the Church of Saint Vaast (on the left). The city center was recently rebuilt to offer more comfortable amenities for tourists. During the summer people can come on boat to enjoy these new shops. In fact, it is only a thirty-minute boat ride on the Deule from Lille.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190407_170302.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"This is the nave of the Church Saint Vaast. This Church actually replaced an earlier church that had grown too small to accommodate the growing town of Wambrechies due to the textile industry growth. As a result, the mayor of the city at the time, the viscount Martel Obert de Quevy, had the Church rebuilt in 1868 in neo-gothic style.\" data-attachment-id=\"4380\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"This is the nave of the Church Saint Vaast. This Church actually replaced an earlier church that had grown too small to accommodate the growing town of Wambrechies due to the textile industry growth. As a result, the mayor of the city at the time, the viscount Martel Obert de Quevy, had the Church rebuilt in 1868 in neo-gothic style.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/06\/20190407_170302\/4117246762.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">This is the nave of the Church Saint Vaast. This Church actually replaced an earlier church that had grown too small to accommodate the growing town of Wambrechies due to the textile industry growth. As a result, the mayor of the city at the time, the viscount Martel Obert de Quevy, had the Church rebuilt in 1868 in neo-gothic style.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190407_170003.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"A large portion of the windows of the Church were destroyed due to the Second World War. The rebuilt versions are nonetheless gorgeous.\" data-attachment-id=\"4388\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"A large portion of the windows of the Church were destroyed due to the Second World War. The rebuilt versions are nonetheless gorgeous.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/06\/20190407_170003\/1874526364.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">A large portion of the windows of the Church were destroyed due to the Second World War. The rebuilt versions are nonetheless gorgeous.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/20190407_170151.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"I simply find this statue of a saint showing his leg quite amusing and wanted to share. (The figure represented by this statue is St. Roch who tended to those attained by the plague until he himself fell ill, shown here pointing to his first plague blister. Legend has it that he retreated into the forest and was kept alive and even healed by a hunting dog that brought him bread.)\" data-attachment-id=\"4379\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"I simply find this statue of a saint showing his leg quite amusing and wanted to share. (The figure represented by this statue is St. Roch who tended to those attained by the plague until he himself fell ill, shown here pointing to his first plague blister. Legend has it that he retreated into the forest and was kept alive and even healed by a hunting dog that brought him bread.)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/06\/20190407_170151\/374451946.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">I simply find this statue of a saint showing his leg quite amusing and wanted to share. (The figure represented by this statue is St. Roch who tended to those attained by the plague until he himself fell ill, shown here pointing to his first plague blister. Legend has it that he retreated into the forest and was kept alive and even healed by a hunting dog that brought him bread.)<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><\/div>\r\n\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"su-tabs-pane su-u-clearfix su-u-trim\" data-title=\"Pas de Calais\">\n<style type=\"text\/css\">\r\n\t#foogallery-gallery-3684 .fg-image {\r\n        width: 150px;\r\n    }\r\n<\/style>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"foogallery foogallery-container foogallery-default foogallery-lightbox-foobox fg-gutter-10 fg-center fg-default fg-light fg-border-thin fg-shadow-outline fg-loading-default fg-loaded-fade-in fg-caption-hover fg-hover-fade fg-hover-zoom fg-ready\" id=\"foogallery-gallery-3684\" data-foogallery=\"{&quot;item&quot;:{&quot;showCaptionTitle&quot;:true,&quot;showCaptionDescription&quot;:true},&quot;lazy&quot;:true}\" >\r\n\t<div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/11\/20181029_125520.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Our Lady of Lorette (or &lt;i&gt;Notre-Dame-de-Lorette&lt;\/i&gt; in French) is the largest military cemetery in France. It is the location of the first major struggle in the north of France during the Great War. The struggle took place from October 1914 until the end of 1915. Securing this region was essential in order to secure the power supply that came from the nearby mines. The Basilica and the accompanying tower were designed by Louis-Marie Cordonnier (who also designed the Opera and the Chamber of Commerce buildings in Lille) and were inaugurated in 1925.\" data-attachment-id=\"3702\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Our Lady of Lorette (or &lt;i&gt;Notre-Dame-de-Lorette&lt;\/i&gt; in French) is the largest military cemetery in France. It is the location of the first major struggle in the north of France during the Great War. The struggle took place from October 1914 until the end of 1915. Securing this region was essential in order to secure the power supply that came from the nearby mines. The Basilica and the accompanying tower were designed by Louis-Marie Cordonnier (who also designed the Opera and the Chamber of Commerce buildings in Lille) and were inaugurated in 1925.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/11\/20181029_125520\/2692689445.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Our Lady of Lorette (or <i>Notre-Dame-de-Lorette<\/i> in French) is the largest military cemetery in France. It is the location of the first major struggle in the north of France during the Great War. The struggle took place from October 1914 until the end of 1915. Securing this region was essential in order to secure the power supply that came from the nearby mines. The Basilica and the accompanying tower were designed by Louis-Marie Cordonnier (who also designed the Opera and the Chamber of Commerce buildings in Lille) and were inaugurated in 1925.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/11\/20181029_124257.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The Tower sits right in front of the Basilica and houses the eternal flame of remembrance.\" data-attachment-id=\"3701\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The Tower sits right in front of the Basilica and houses the eternal flame of remembrance.\" width=\"150\" he